      <h2>📍 Today's Watch List</h2>
      <ul>
      <li>Vantage/VoltaGrid: the groups' injunction reply Nov. 23, their response to the motion to dismiss Dec. 7 (defendants' reply Dec. 14), whether the U.S. attorney general weighs in on the constitutional question, and the Jan. 11 pretrial conference.</li>
      <li>TCEQ: which data center permits follow SpaceX's now that reviews have restarted, including any for on-site gas plants in the eight tracked DFW counties.</li>
      <li>ChronoScale/STN: HSR clearance, the deal's closing, and what STN says about the Odessa campus's generation and air permitting.</li>
      <li>Dallas: the council committee's first look at data center rules, and whether Joppa residents get a hearing.</li>
      <li>PUC open meeting today; the Large Load Working Group and Batch/CTP Workshop 4b also meet today. Project 59999's Texas Register notice runs Nov. 20, with comments due Dec. 14.</li>
      <li>ERCOT's Dec. 10 community impact report, and whether projects that didn't respond drop out of Batch Zero, as Garza expects.</li>
      <li>Hillsboro: whether the unnamed company signs a land contract or asks for city services.</li>
      <li>Lavon's moratorium and Elevon North annexation outcomes, and Brazos County's RELLIS vote, still unreported.</li>
      <li>Starbase's Dec. 9 abatement hearing; Georgetown City Council's Dec. 8 vote on Inner Loop Exchange.</li>
      <li>Docket 60332: the PUC's issues order and whether it goes to a contested hearing.</li>
      <li>Batch Zero complaints, paused until Nov. 30; the ERCOT board Dec. 7–8; the PUC's Dec. 17 meeting on the audit.</li>
      </ul>

